prompt:
The image is a 60 mm x 60 mm patch of skin with a millimetre ruler printed along its bottom edge.
The dark spot is 2 mm across and 15% darker than the surrounding skin. Lighting is normal indoor. For an observer with perfect 20/20 vision looking straight at it, what is the farthest distance in metres at which the spot can still be seen?
Reply with JSON only, in this shape: {"distance_m": n, "reasoning_short": "..."}
